Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P10.6 follow-up: the page-turn prompt "L1" / "R1" follows switch_glyphs

Design: docs/P10.6_GLYPHS.md ("Page-turn prompt"). The item shop, the field
menu's item list and a few other menus (card shop, Digimon Lab, battle menu,
name entry, training) print the page-turn prompt as the plain letters of the
string `L1` / `R1` (bytes 19 05 / 1F 05) in a size-1 text window, next to a
blinking wedge sprite; it is font text, not one of the 114 icons, so the cell
patch of port/options/switch_glyphs.c never touched it.

`textWindowSetSubString` (the one place `setString` resolves a table string)
hands the string to `dw3_port_text_override` with the window's style. The port
returns the string unchanged unless the window is a size-1 window, the string is
exactly `L1` or `R1`, `switch_glyphs` is on and the button map gives that PS
button a Switch glyph; then it returns a two-byte icon string (`01 n`) that
draws the glyph from two spare 12x12 cells the port adds to the size-1 icon
table. With the option off the call returns its argument at once: the text, the
table and the picture are those of main. The wedge sprite is not touched.

--- a/src/engine/text/text_window.c
+++ b/src/engine/text/text_window.c
@@ -148,6 +148,10 @@
         if (str == NULL) {
             return;
         }
+#if PORT_HOST
+        /* P10.6: a page-turn prompt ("L1" / "R1") becomes the Switch glyph's icon string */
+        str = (char *)dw3_port_text_override(obj->style, str);
+#endif
         setTextBuffer(obj, &obj->text[index], str);
     } else {
         setTextBuffer(obj, &obj->text[index], text);
